# Packaging integrity only. This file changes no scientific content, no review
# verdict, no recommendation, no estimand, no threshold, and no governance status.
#
# Two packets in this tree record SHA-256 values over the working-tree bytes of
# Markdown files in this directory. Without an eol attribute, Git materializes
# those files according to each machine's core.autocrlf setting, so the same
# commit yields different working-tree bytes on Windows and on Linux and the
# recorded values stop matching. Three files here were checked out CRLF on the
# authoring machine for exactly that reason:
#
#   DSR_AGENT_REVIEW_ADDENDUM.md
#   DSR_DRAFT_REVIEW_PACKET.md
#   DSR_METHOD_PREREGISTRATION_DRAFT.md
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the working-tree bytes equal the index blob on every
# platform, so a reviewer can verify either way and get the same answer. The
# index blobs are unchanged by this file; only the working-tree materialization
# changes.
#
# Added on owner instruction, applying the remedy proposed under C-1 in
# v1.1-method-candidate/README.md section 5. It mirrors the .gitattributes in
# external-review-packet/ and in v1.1-method-candidate/, which are the existing
# precedent. The recorded hashes affected by it are re-recorded in the same
# commit, in both packets, with the pre-pin values preserved rather than erased.

*.md            text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
